    "lem-direct-sums-and-tensor-products-of-finite-dimensional-unitary-representations": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-matrix-coefficient-of-a-unitary-representation",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\pi:G\\to U(H)$ be a group homomorphism and let $\\xi,\\eta\\in H$. Its **matrix coefficient** associated with $(\\xi,\\eta)$ is $$c_{\\xi,\\eta}:G\\to\\mathbb C,\\qquad c_{\\xi,\\eta}(g)=\\langle\\pi(g)\\xi,\\eta\\rangle.$$ We use the convention that the Hilbert pairing is linear in its first argument and conjugate-linear in its second. Thus $c_{\\xi,\\eta}$ is linear in $\\xi$ and conjugate-linear in $\\eta$.",
