          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement and proof: The zero vector is not an eigenvector; step 1.1 assumes \u2016v\u2016=1, and step 2.1 uses L\u00b2(R)\u2260{0} to force a nonzero summand."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement and proof: One-dimensionality is the crux: step 1.1 shows every irreducible subrepresentation of the abelian group R would be one-dimensional, spanned by a unit eigenvector."
        },
        {
